# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need. Both are gitignored; this file is not.
#
# Anything already set in your shell wins over this file, so a one-off
# `PI_STASIS_MODE=off npm run experiment ...` still overrides what is here.
# Values are literal — no ${VAR} interpolation, no shell evaluation.
#
# Read by: npm run experiment, scripts/smoke-trial.ts, and a live `pi` session
# (which takes only the PI_STASIS_* variables, and never alters its own environment).

# --- Credentials -----------------------------------------------------------
# Needed to run a study against a real model. Alternatively run `pi` once and
# `/login openrouter`, which stores a token Pi finds on its own.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# The provider comes from the benchmark YAML, not from here. If you point a
# benchmark at another provider, set that provider's key instead.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Physiology ------------------------------------------------------------
# Named parameter set from config/profiles/. One of: balanced, risk-averse,
# exploratory, high-persistence, stress-sensitive, fast-recovery.
# PI_STASIS_PROFILE=balanced

# active   physiology runs, influences the agent, enforcement on
# static   frozen at baseline, still injected, constant policy
# observer records everything, influences nothing — the control condition
# off      nothing
# PI_STASIS_MODE=active

# An extra YAML overlay, applied after the project and user overlays.
# PI_STASIS_CONFIG=/path/to/overlay.yaml

# --- Session behaviour -----------------------------------------------------
# panel | status | off
# PI_STASIS_DISPLAY=panel

# Only "0" is honoured; anything else leaves enforcement on.
# PI_STASIS_ENFORCE=0

# Only "1" is honoured. Upgrades suspected bash bypasses from logged to blocked.
# PI_STASIS_GUARD_BASH=1

# Only "0" is honoured. Turns off the JSONL telemetry that makes a run reconstructible.
# PI_STASIS_TELEMETRY=0

# Defaults to .pi/stasis/telemetry
# PI_STASIS_TELEMETRY_DIR=

# --- Harness ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Only "1" is honoured. Substitutes a scripted agent for the real model, which
# validates the whole study pipeline at no cost. Leaving this set in a file is a
# good way to run a worthless study that looks healthy, so the runner warns when
# it finds it here rather than in your shell.
# PI_STASIS_FAUX=1

# scripts/smoke-trial.ts only.
# PI_STASIS_SMOKE_PROVIDER=openrouter
# PI_STASIS_SMOKE_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5
# PI_STASIS_SMOKE_TURNS=20
# PI_STASIS_SMOKE_TIMEOUT=300

# --- Loading ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Read this file instead of the conventional .env / .env.local.
# PI_STASIS_ENV_FILE=/path/to/other.env

# Only "1" is honoured. Ignore .env files entirely, as `--no-env-file` does.
# PI_STASIS_NO_ENV_FILE=1
